This function works by repeatedly dividing `n` by 3 until it becomes less than 1. If at any point `n` is less than 1, then `n` is not a power of three and the function returns `false`. If `n` is exactly 1, then `n` itself is a power of three and the function returns `true`.

The time complexity of this function is O(log(n)) because we divide `n` by 3 in each iteration until it becomes less than 1. The space complexity is O(1) because we only use a constant amount of extra memory to store the intermediate value of `n`.

